GETUID(2)                      P32W Unix                       GETUID(2)

NAME
       getuid, geteuid, getgid, getegid - get user and group identity

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       uid_t getuid(void);
       uid_t geteuid(void);
       gid_t getgid(void);
       gid_t getegid(void);

DESCRIPTION
       getuid and getgid return the real user and group IDs: those
       of the user who logged in (login(1) sets them; su(1)
       changes them). geteuid and getegid return the effective
       IDs, which differ from the real ones while a set-user-ID or
       set-group-ID program runs (exec(2)). Permission checks use
       the effective IDs; access(2) uses the real ones.

RETURN VALUE
       The ID asked for. These calls cannot fail.

SEE ALSO
       setuid(2), exec(2), access(2), id(1), whoami(1), passwd(5)
